# App backup with live mesh keys (NetKey/AppKey/DevKeys) — never commit
ios/
# Downloaded APK + decompile output (large, redistributable? no)
android/*.xapk
android/xapk/
android/jadx-out/
android/jadx.log
__pycache__/
.venv/
dist/
build/
.coverage
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
# The CLI's per-address sequence counters (+ their .lock / .bak / temp siblings) and the device keys `provision`
# writes — never commit, never share
tools/.jhmesh_state*
tools/.jhmesh_devkey*
# the temporary file an atomic write renames into place (`.<name>.<pid>.<thread>.tmp`)
tools/..jhmesh_*
.claude/worktrees/
# What the docs tell you to create in the repository root: app exports (every mesh key), decoded captures (a day
# of decrypted household traffic), hop matrices, `tee` logs, editor/HA backup copies. Fixtures under tests/ are
# tracked explicitly and matched by none of these.
/JungHome*.json
/MeshNetwork*.json
/android/*.json
*.bak
/hops.json
*.ndjson
*.pcap
*.pcapng
capture-*.log
.hypothesis/
